From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: expose ThinkSmart amplifier mute GPIO

Use the standard plural GPIO property consumed by the codec driver so it
can control the connected mute line. Preserve the board's existing polarity.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/msm8953-mainline/linux
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7
Related codec-source credits: drivers/tas5782m/README.md in the device tree.


---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
index da70c94a9c35c80495e9e6582469e86d8f468281..82a5a6de6d000ed3664ea0796715717d028c555b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -269,8 +269,8 @@
 		reg = <0x49>;
 
 		pdn-gpios = <&tlmm 44 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-		/* The next two GPIOs are connected but unused by the driver */
-		mute-gpio = <&tlmm 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		mute-gpios = <&tlmm 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		/* Fault indication is not used by the driver. */
 		fault-gpio = <&tlmm 45 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pvdd-supply = <&speaker_amp_pvdd>;
 
